### Page 1 of 3

```text
PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
Due to the Martin Luther King Jr. holiday, a meeting of the Public Services Committee was instead
held on Tuesday. January 20, 2026, in City Council Chambers and via electronic meeting, stalling
at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS:
Dr. Mark Rinne, Acting Chairman; Dr. Michelle Aldrich; Pete
Laybourn, and Mark Moody. Absent: Dr. Kathy Emmons, Chairwoman.
AGENDA ITEMS
10.
ORDINANCE —3 READING
— Creating Chapter
1.28, Administrative Inspection
Warrants, establishing authority for their issuance, and amending the Municipal Code of
the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, to authorize certain city officials, as specified, to apply
for administrative inspection warrants.
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 31 and final reading, seconded by Mr. Moody.
Dr. Aldrich
moved to postpone until the February 9, 2026 meeting of the governing body, seconded by Mr.
Moody. Motion to postpone carried by unanimous voice vote.
John Brodie, City Attorney, provided a staff report and advised at the request of Chief Andrew
Dykshorn, Fire Rescue Department, and Antony Pomerleau, Chief Building Inspector, a substitute
was circulated.
Upon inquiry, Mr. Pomerleau provided information related to the urgency of
approval of the proposed ordinance. Committee members Aldrich, Layboum, and Moody
commented on the item. Public comments were made by Phillip Bowling; Gary Chadwick, Board
of Realtors; Patricia McCoy; Stephen Jacobson; Ben Rayl; and Kathy Seigliano.
11.
ORDINANCE _2nd READING
Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, various
tracts of land completely surrounded by current City limits situate in eastern Cheyenne,
generally located south of Storey Boulevard, east of Powderhouse Road, north of Dell
Range Boulevard, and west of Ridge Road. (SPONSOR
— DR. EMMONS)
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2h1d reading, seconded by Mr. Moody. Motion to approve carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department. provided a staffreport. Committec members
Laybourn and Moody commented on the item.
12.
ORDINANCE —2 READING
-- Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne. establishing the zoning classifications of AG
— Agricultural, and MR
—
Medium-Density Residential, for land annexed to the City of Cheyenne generally located
south of Storey Boulevard, east ofPowderhouse Road, north of Dell Range Boulevard, and
west of Ridge Road. (SPONSOR
— DR. EMMONS)
```

