```text
Dr. Aldrich moved to approve on 2 reading, seconded by Mr. Moody. Motion to approve carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and committee
members Aldrich commented on the item.
13.
ORDINANCE —2” READING
— Amending 5.7.3 Accessory Dwelling Units of the
Cheyenne Unified Development Code to remove owner-occupancy and adjust parking
requirements for Accessory Dwellings, and making conforming amendments to the
definitions
of an
Accessory
Dwelling
and
Semi-Attached
Dwelling
under
1.4.4
Descriptions of Uses of Land and Buildings. (SPONSOR- MR. MOODY)
Mr. Moody moved to approve on 2t,d reading, seconded by Mr. Layboum. Motion carried with Mr.
Layboum and Mr. Moody voting “YES” and Dr. Aldrich voting “NO.”
Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report. Committee members
Aldrich and Moody commented on the item. Public comment was made by Dan Dorsch, Habitat
for Humanity of Laramie County Executive Director.
18.
RESOLUTION
— Authorizing the Mayor and City Clerk to sign a Final Plat for Cheyenne
Business Parkway, I 5th Filing, City of Cheyenne, Laramie County, Wyoming, located east
of Echostar Drive and south of and adjacent to Campstool Road. (SPONSOR
— DR.
EMMONS)
Dr. Aldrich moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Moody. Motion to approve carried by unanimous
voice vote.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and Casey Palma,
agent for the owner, provided additional information.
19.
RESOLUTION
— Certifying compliance with Wyoming Statute § 15-1-402 for the City-
initiated annexation of various tracts of land completely surrounded by current City limits
situate in western and southern Cheyenne generally located cast of 1-25, south of the
intersection of Westland Road and Missile Drive, north of West and East Allison Road and
east of and adjacent to North College Drive. (SPONSOR
— DR. EMMONS)
Mr. Laybourn moved to adopt. Motion died from the lack of a second.
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report. Chairman Rinne
and committee member Aldrich commented on the item.
21.
PRELIMINARY PLATS:
a)
Preliminary Plat for Dry Creek Vista, City of Cheyenne, Laramie County,
Wyoming, located northeast of the intersection of Frank Court and Rock Springs
Street.
